<qti-assessment-item xmlns="http://www.imsglobal.org/xsd/imsqtiasi_v3p0" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.imsglobal.org/xsd/imsqtiasi_v3p0 https://purl.imsglobal.org/spec/qti/v3p0/schema/xsd/imsqti_asiv3p0_v1p0.xsd" identifier="pcb-item-77ba62234ce9488d971310a13319994e" title="sat-c2-u20-secularization.html qc1" adaptive="true" time-dependent="false">
  <qti-response-declaration identifier="RESPONSE" cardinality="single" base-type="identifier">
    <qti-correct-response><qti-value>D</qti-value></qti-correct-response>
  </qti-response-declaration>
  <qti-outcome-declaration identifier="SCORE" cardinality="single" base-type="float"><qti-default-value><qti-value>0</qti-value></qti-default-value></qti-outcome-declaration>
  <qti-outcome-declaration identifier="FEEDBACK" cardinality="single" base-type="identifier"/>
  <qti-outcome-declaration identifier="INTERACTION_VISIBILITY" cardinality="single" base-type="identifier">
    <qti-default-value><qti-value>show_interaction</qti-value></qti-default-value>
  </qti-outcome-declaration>
  <qti-item-body>
    <qti-feedback-block identifier="show_interaction" outcome-identifier="INTERACTION_VISIBILITY" show-hide="show" class="qti-margin-0">
      <qti-content-body>
        <p>Which sentence uses &quot;secularization&quot; correctly?</p>
    <qti-choice-interaction response-identifier="RESPONSE" shuffle="true" max-choices="1">
      <qti-simple-choice identifier="A">The bishop performed the town&apos;s entire secularization in a single twenty-minute ceremony, sprinkling blessed water on the new courthouse steps while the council watched.</qti-simple-choice><qti-simple-choice identifier="B">Food critics across the city mourned the sudden secularization of the famous tasting menu after the new chef stripped every last spice from the winter dishes.</qti-simple-choice><qti-simple-choice identifier="C">The planning committee praised the careful secularization of its own minutes, which kept every important decision hidden from the public eye for a full decade.</qti-simple-choice><qti-simple-choice identifier="D">The museum&apos;s timeline of secularization ran from 1790 to 1905: civil registries replacing parish rolls, then lay schoolteachers, then oath-taking moved from altar to magistrate.</qti-simple-choice>
    </qti-choice-interaction>
      </qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>

    <qti-feedback-block identifier="FB-A" outcome-identifier="FEEDBACK" show-hide="show">
      <qti-content-body><p>Not quite! Secularization is a slow transfer of institutions out of religion&apos;s control, so it can&apos;t be performed in twenty minutes — least of all by a bishop blessing the steps, which keeps religion&apos;s hand on the courthouse rather than lifting it.</p></qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>
    <qti-feedback-block identifier="FB-B" outcome-identifier="FEEDBACK" show-hide="show">
      <qti-content-body><p>Not quite! Secularization concerns religion&apos;s authority over institutions, not flavor — a menu losing its spices has lost seasoning, and &apos;secular&apos; has never meant bland.</p></qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>
    <qti-feedback-block identifier="FB-C" outcome-identifier="FEEDBACK" show-hide="show">
      <qti-content-body><p>Not quite! Secular means belonging to the present, public world, not hidden from it — a committee concealing its minutes for a decade is practicing secrecy, and the sound-alike is the whole trap here.</p></qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>
    <qti-feedback-block identifier="FB-D" outcome-identifier="FEEDBACK" show-hide="show">
      <qti-content-body><p>Correct! Secularization is institutions passing out of religion&apos;s hands into worldly ones, and this timeline is that process step by step: registries, schoolteachers, and oaths each moving from parish to civil authority across a century.</p></qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>
  </qti-item-body>
  <qti-response-processing>
